course: dictionary
lesson: 14186
title: Mopping and its many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning. Mopping is a good example. Its main meaning is cleaning a floor with a mop and water. «Dad is mopping the kitchen floor after dinner.» The mop and the floor are the clues, so you know what kind of mopping it is.
explain: Mopping can also mean wiping something, such as sweat, with a cloth. «Mopping his brow, Sam ran on to finish the race.» His brow is his forehead, and he is wiping the sweat from it. The race tells you he is hot and tired, not cleaning anything.
explain: Mopping up can mean cleaning up spilled liquid, or finishing the last parts of a job. «Please mop up the juice before it drips on the carpet.» The juice has spilled, so mop up means clean it up. Read the words around the word to pick the right meaning.
fact: Mopping is the -ing form of the verb mop: mop, mops, mopped, mopping.
fact: «Mopping» means cleaning a floor with a mop and water.
fact: «Mopping his brow» means wiping sweat from the forehead.
fact: «Mopping up» means cleaning up spilled liquid or finishing the last parts of a job.
fact: A floor is slippery after mopping, so people put up a «Wet floor» sign to warn others.
exercise: «Dad is mopping the kitchen floor.» What is Dad doing? | *Cleaning the floor with a mop and water | Painting the kitchen walls | Cooking the dinner
exercise: «Sam kept mopping his brow in the hot sun.» What is Sam wiping from his brow? | Crumbs | Paint | *Sweat | Rain
exercise: «Please mop up the juice before it drips.» What does mop up mean here? | Eat the juice | Hide the juice | *Clean up the spilled juice | Stir the juice
test: «The wet floor is slippery after mopping.» Why is there a sign? | *Because people could slip and fall on the wet floor | Because the sign is pretty | Because the floor is dirty and needs a bath | Because the floor is made of wood
test: Which meaning fits «mopping up the spilled milk»? | Wiping sweat from a face | Finishing a race | Writing a list | *Cleaning up spilled liquid
exam: Which sentence uses mopping to mean wiping tears? | The mop is in the cupboard | *Mopping her tears, Mia smiled at last | Mopping takes a long time | Mopping the floor is hard work
